<Base title="Privacy" description="Privacy information for this directory.">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p>Last updated: 2026-11-11.</p>
  <h2>What this site collects</h2>
  <p>This site has no accounts, no ads and no sale of data. Browsing it requires no personal information. The only way personal information reaches us is if you send a correction or removal request (see below).</p>
  <h2>Google Analytics (GA4)</h2>
  <p>We use Google Analytics 4 to measure aggregate traffic. It sets cookies and sends usage data to Google: pages viewed, approximate location, device and browser type, and the page that referred you. Google acts as our processor for this data. We do not enable Google signals or ad personalization, we use the shortest data retention setting offered, we do not set user IDs, and we do not put personal data in events or URLs. You can opt out with the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics opt-out add-on</a>. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a> for how Google handles this data.</p>
  <h2>Google Search Console</h2>
  <p>We use Google Search Console to see aggregate search performance (queries, impressions, clicks). It gives us no data about individual visitors.</p>
  <h2>Search on this site</h2>
  <p>Site search (Pagefind) runs in your browser. Your search terms are not sent to us or to anyone else.</p>
  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>The site is hosted on Vercel, which keeps standard server logs (such as IP address and requested page) for operating and securing the service.</p>
  <h2>Correction and removal requests</h2>
  <p>If you ask us to correct or remove a listing, by email or through a correction form once one is published, we receive the name, role and email address you give us and the evidence you provide. We use them only to check the request and reply to you. We do not publish them or sell them. The service that hosts any form will be named on this page before the form goes live. We plan to delete a request's contact details 12 months after the request is closed. The public data only records that a removal happened (a suppression record without requester details).</p>
  <h2>Business information in the directory</h2>
  <p>The directory lists only business information that businesses have published publicly, such as company name, website, business address and fees, with the source and dates shown for each fact. To correct or remove a listing, see <a href="/about/#corrections">corrections</a>.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>The contact address is on the <a href="/about/#corrections">About page</a>.</p>
</Base>
